# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Keke Song et al. (2024). General-purpose machine-learned potential for 16 elemental metals and their alloys.
#   Nature Communications. doi:10.1038/s41467-024-54554-x  arXiv:2311.04732v2
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2311.04732v2 (sha256 16258f262108f916...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 243 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/song2024.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the UNEP-v1 model (NEP4, trained with the multi-loss
# SNES algorithm introduced here) on 1- and 2-component data of 16 metals,
# with its training RMSEs, test force RMSEs on three multi-component
# public data sets and formation-energy MAEs on Materials Project ternaries
# and GNoME structures (Results), and its MD speed (Table I). Property
# comparisons with EAM (Fig. 3, Tables S1-S4) and the MPEA applications are
# not encoded.

